 **(MEAS-D) Joint measurability of the potential records.** Fix n, p_raw and the options, and assume EX-A. On the Borel set of valid inputs, the following objects of the potential fit P° (`W3-AUDIT-A:GW`) are Borel functions of (X^r, y^r, U^{(0)}, …, U^{(13)}), the seed entering only as a label: the calibration record 𝓒° and the event 𝒜°; the records of the four final islands, with the sets 𝓜_r of models they evaluate; the final local-search and LS0 archives and the final-run ledger, hence 𝓜, 𝒯, Ŝ and every statistical field of P°'s output; the output event 𝒪°; and Z, π, π₀. Moreover 0 < Z ≤ κ_n for every valid data set, with κ_n depending on n only, so 1_{𝒜°}Z, 1_{𝒜°}Ẑ and 1_{𝒜°}Ẑ_r·H_r(h), for every bounded h of §2, are integrable under the joint law of §0, for every law of the data. Consequently, under the joint law of §0 (H-U/SI, :29 and :35-36, which together make each final stream independent of the pair (data, streams 0–9)), for each island r every identity or bound of §2 about island r stated "given 𝓒 on 𝒜" holds, for the potential pair (𝒜°, 𝓒°), conditionally on (data, 𝓒°); so do the statements obtained from these by finite sums, monotone comparison and union bounds over r, which is all that the joint-law clauses of §2 use; and where a clause assumes IND-T, the same holds for functions of the four final streams jointly. Nothing is claimed about the actual 𝒜, 𝒪 or the guard, which enter only through the pathwise inclusions of `W3-AUDIT-A:GW` (GW-iii), (GW-iv). (Proof: `lemmas/MEAS_D.md`.)
 
 Conventions: off 𝒜° the final-run objects are set to a fixed symbol ⊥ (as 𝓒° := ⊥ when the calibration is not called). "Borel" is with respect to the product σ-field on the streams; each object depends on finitely many of their coordinates.
+
+*Remark (actual runs; not part of any claim).* The guard's clock is not modelled (`W3-AUDIT-A:GW`, "Not claimed"). A probability of an actual-run event, that is, one intersected with {completed} or with the actual 𝒜, is therefore read as an outer probability unless the clock is taken jointly measurable with the streams; in either reading it is bounded by the probability of the corresponding potential event.
